<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="051" project="ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Record→analysis 1:N + Analysis subgrid/tab on Matter/Project forms</title>
    <phase>5 Entry model + record integration</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Net-new Dataverse relationship model (record→analysis 1:N) + form customization; regarding-integrity is a correctness invariant (single-valued, NFR-05); realizes the §12.2 record-integration model.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully-specified Dataverse forms/relationship work over the owner-created regarding field-set (task 012); no novel design — subgrid config + relationship wiring against a known contract.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P5a</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Dataverse form/relationship surface — distinct file set from the frontend routing (050) and launch-resolver work; no shared code.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>012</deps>
    <tags>dataverse, forms, ribbon</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Realize the record→analysis 1:N model (spec §12.2 / FR-15): a Matter and a Project form each show a subgrid (or tab)
    of the analyses whose matching regarding field equals that record. A record has many analyses; each Analysis belongs
    to exactly one record via exactly one populated regarding field (single-valued, ADR-024 / NFR-05). This is 100%
    net-new — no `sprk_analysis` subgrid and no record→analysis 1:N exist today (§13.4). Consume the owner-created
    regarding field-set from task 012; do not author new columns.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Dataverse model-driven form customization (subgrids/tabs), 1:N relationships,
    and the RegardingResolver single-valued regarding field-set (ADR-024). Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    The `sprk_matter` and `sprk_project` main forms each show a subgrid/tab listing the `sprk_analysis` records whose
    matching regarding lookup (`sprk_regardingmatter` / `sprk_regardingproject`) equals the open record; the record→analysis
    relationship is 1:N (a record has many analyses, an analysis belongs to exactly one record via one populated regarding
    field); the subgrid launches/opens analyses per the entry matrix (2b/2d wired in task 052).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      §13.4: no form has a `sprk_analysis` subgrid/tab today and no record→analysis 1:N wiring exists — `sprk_analysis`'s
      only lookups are `_sprk_documentid_value` + `sprk_Playbook`. The §12.2 model (record shows a subgrid of its analyses;
      an analysis belongs to one record) requires the owner-created regarding field-set (`sprk_regardingmatter`,
      `sprk_regardingproject`, `sprk_regardingdocument`) consumed via RegardingResolver in task 012, plus subgrids added to
      the parent forms here. NFR-05 / ADR-024: exactly one populated regarding field per Analysis (single-valued regarding),
      giving a clean 1:N.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">sprk_matter main form (subgrid/tab of analyses)</file>
      <file role="modify">sprk_project main form (subgrid/tab of analyses)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">the RegardingResolver single-valued regarding field-set consumed in task 012 (sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingproject / sprk_regardingdocument)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/data-model/ (sprk_analysis regarding contract)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="012" status="pending">Consumes `sprk_worktype` + the single-valued regarding field-set (RegardingResolver) — the lookups the subgrid filters on.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">SCOPE: the record→analysis relationship — exactly ONE regarding field is populated per Analysis (single-valued); the subgrid filters on the matching regarding lookup. MUST NOT model multi-record ownership of a single Analysis.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: this task consumes owner-created columns only — MUST NOT author new `sprk_analysis` columns or option sets; the regarding field-set + `sprk_worktype` exist per the schema contract (spec Prerequisites).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-05">SCOPE: regarding integrity — the 1:N is clean (record has many analyses; analysis belongs to exactly one record via one populated regarding field). Multi-populated regarding on a single Analysis is rejected/invalid.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: subgrid launch/open behavior defers to the entry matrix (2b/2d) wired in task 052 via `openSpaarkeAi` — this task lays the subgrid + relationship; it MUST NOT hand-roll a `surfaceLaunchRegistry` open (ADR-039).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-FIELD-MAPPING-FRAMEWORK.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="RegardingResolver single-valued regarding" location="src/client/pcf/RegardingResolver">
        The regarding field-set is single-valued (exactly one populated); the parent record supplies the source parent. The subgrid on the parent form filters `sprk_analysis` by the matching regarding lookup.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; load ADR-024, ADR-039; confirm the owner-created regarding field-set + `sprk_worktype` are present (task 012 output / schema preflight).</step>
    <step order="1">Establish the record→analysis 1:N: the `sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingmatter` → `sprk_matter` and `sprk_analysis.sprk_regardingproject` → `sprk_project` lookups are the 1:N relationships that back the subgrids.</step>
    <step order="2">Add an Analyses subgrid/tab to the `sprk_matter` main form filtered to analyses where `sprk_regardingmatter` = the open record.</step>
    <step order="3">Add an Analyses subgrid/tab to the `sprk_project` main form filtered to analyses where `sprk_regardingproject` = the open record.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify single-valued regarding: each Analysis shows under exactly one parent record (one populated regarding); confirm no Analysis appears under two records.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm the subgrid open/launch path defers to `openSpaarkeAi` (task 052), not `surfaceLaunchRegistry`.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set task 051 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in projects/ai-advanced-capabilities-analysis-hub-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a legitimate need for an Analysis to belong to more than one record surfaces (multi-populated regarding), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6.5 (ADR-024 single-valued regarding) — do not silently model multi-record ownership or add a second populated regarding.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>None — §13.4 (design-discussion.md:361) confirms no form has a `sprk_analysis` subgrid/tab today and no record→analysis 1:N wiring exists; `sprk_analysis`'s only lookups are `_sprk_documentid_value` + `sprk_Playbook`.</existing>
    <extension>No — there is no existing record→analysis relationship or subgrid to extend; the regarding field-set (owner-created, consumed in 012) is the enabling contract, but the 1:N + subgrids on the parent forms do not exist and must be added.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Matter/Project record cannot show or launch its own analyses; the §12.2 record-integration model (and entry cases 2b/2d) is unrealizable — records and analyses stay unlinked in the UI.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="pac">Dataverse solution / form customization (export/import).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">sprk_matter main form — Analyses subgrid/tab</output>
    <output type="config">sprk_project main form — Analyses subgrid/tab</output>
    <output type="config">record→analysis 1:N relationships (sprk_regardingmatter, sprk_regardingproject)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `sprk_matter` record with N analyses regarding it, when the form opens, then the Analyses subgrid lists exactly those N analyses (filtered by `sprk_regardingmatter`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `sprk_project` record, when the form opens, then its Analyses subgrid lists the analyses whose `sprk_regardingproject` = the record.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record can have many analyses (1:N); each Analysis appears under exactly one parent record (single-valued regarding).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an Analysis with a second populated regarding field is invalid/rejected — a single Analysis does NOT appear under two records (multi-record ownership rejected per ADR-024 / NFR-05).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the subgrid open path uses the entry-matrix `openSpaarkeAi` route (task 052), not `surfaceLaunchRegistry`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No new `sprk_analysis` columns/option sets were authored by this task (owner-created contract consumed only).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec §12.2 / FR-15 / §13.4. Depends on the owner-created regarding field-set consumed in task 012. Subgrid
    open/launch wiring lands in task 052 (`openSpaarkeAi` ribbon launcher). Completion summary appended here when done.

    COMPLETED 2026-07-29.

    **1:N relationships**: confirmed already live (no new relationship authored, per §11 reuse-first). Verified via
    Dataverse Web API `EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='sprk_matter')/OneToManyRelationships` (and `sprk_project`
    equivalent), filtered to `ReferencingEntity eq 'sprk_analysis'`:
    - `sprk_analysis_RegardingMatter_sprk_matter` — ReferencingAttribute `sprk_regardingmatter`
    - `sprk_analysis_RegardingProject_sprk_project` — ReferencingAttribute `sprk_regardingproject`
    Both auto-created the moment the owner added the two lookup columns (task 010/012 schema prerequisite); this
    task authored no schema.

    **Form customization — applied live, not deferred**: the POML's fallback clause ("if the live subgrid placement
    cannot be fully applied without maker-portal interaction... hand to task 071") did NOT trigger. The Dataverse
    Web API form-customization path (explicitly permitted as an alternative to the ribbon-edit PAC-export/import
    flow) was fully scriptable in this environment:
      1. Located both main forms via `systemform` query (Matter formid `4fa382f2-c273-f011-b4cb-6045bdd6a665`,
         Project formid `5aa00242-5212-f111-8342-7ced8d1dc988`).
      2. Fetched live FormXml via Web API, inspected existing subgrid tabs (`tab_projects`, `tab_todos_sprk_project`,
         `tab_reportcard`, etc.) to mirror the established structural convention exactly (same tab/section/row/cell
         shape, same subgrid classid `{E7A81278-8635-4D9E-8D4D-59480B391C5B}`).
      3. Identified the correct subgrid view via `savedquery` (querytype=2 "Analysis Associated View",
         id `4ef7e264-a43f-4d9c-ad56-e48c561ad30e`) — the canonical Dataverse view for a child-entity subgrid,
         same pattern as every other live subgrid on these two forms.
      4. Authored two new tab fragments (new GUIDs, no collision with any existing tab/control id — checked against
         the full existing tab/control inventory on both forms) and inserted each before its form's `</tabs>` via a
         string-level PATCH — the underlying FormXml is otherwise byte-identical to what was live before.
      5. PATCHed `systemforms({id})` for both forms, then called `PublishXml` (entities: sprk_matter, sprk_project).
      6. Verified post-publish: re-fetched both forms, confirmed `tab_analyses_sprk_matter` /
         `tab_analyses_sprk_project` and the correct `RelationshipName` values are present, and confirmed both
         FormXml documents are still well-formed XML.
      7. Checked-in artifacts (durable record + what 071 should verify rather than re-apply):
         - `src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_matter/FormXml/analyses/matter-analyses-tab.xml`
         - `src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_project/FormXml/analyses/project-analyses-tab.xml`
         (mirrors the existing `matter-reportcard-tab.xml` precedent from `x-matter-performance-KPI-r1` task 044).

    **Deployment note for task 071**: the Analysis subgrid/tab is ALREADY LIVE on both `sprk_matter` and
    `sprk_project` main forms in spaarkedev1 as of this task. Task 071 step 3 ("deploy... the Analysis subgrid/tab
    form customizations") should VERIFY presence (e.g. re-run the same `systemforms` query and grep for
    `tab_analyses_sprk_matter` / `tab_analyses_sprk_project`) rather than re-apply — re-applying would either be a
    no-op (idempotent string search finds the tab already present) or, if attempted via a fresh solution-export/
    import flow, could risk a duplicate-tab conflict. No action needed if the environment is unchanged between now
    and 071's execution.

    **Single-valued regarding invariant**: NOT re-implemented here (out of this task's scope — already enforced at
    the application layer by task 012's `analysisRegardingResolver.ts`, which flags/rejects zero- or multi-populated
    regarding). This task only adds the *display* of the 1:N relationship on the parent forms; Dataverse itself has
    no platform-native mutual-exclusivity constraint across the two lookup columns, so the invariant continues to
    depend on task 012's resolver + write-path discipline (RegardingResolver PCF / PolymorphicResolverService),
    exactly as ADR-024 specifies.

    **Subgrid open path**: no ribbon button, JavaScript, or launch logic was added by this task — the subgrid is a
    stock Dataverse display control with no custom open/launch wiring, so there is nothing here that could violate
    ADR-039 by hard-coding a `surfaceLaunchRegistry`-style open. Task 052 (ribbon launcher / `openSpaarkeAi`) is the
    task that will wire any custom open behavior, per the constraint.

    **Gates**: adr-check (ADR-024, ADR-039) — 0 violations. code-review — both FormXml fragments well-formed
    (validated via XML parse pre- and post-live-publish), no id/name collisions against the full existing
    tab/control inventory on both forms, structure mirrors the live "To Dos" (`tab_todos_sprk_project`) and
    "Report Card" (`tab_reportcard`) precedents exactly. No `.cs`/`.ts`/`.tsx` touched — SpaarkeAi/src/client/shared
    surfaces (owned by task 040) were not modified, per this task's constraint.

    No deviation from the POML's directional steps or escalation trigger (no multi-populated-regarding need
    surfaced).
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load knowledge files. Follow task-execute incl. Step 9.5 gates (FULL: code-review + adr-check).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
